 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The threshold falls between -0.3 V and -0.9 V at -250 μA with the gate tied to the drain. On-resistance is guaranteed at four gate voltages: 43 mΩ max at -4.5 V and 55 mΩ max at -2.5 V (both at -4.0 A), 75 mΩ max at -1.8 V and -2.0 A, and 100 mΩ max at -1.5 V and -1.0 A. The gate is rated ±10 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "On-resistance climbs with junction temperature, to roughly 1.7 times its 25 °C value at 150 °C. Through the transfer curve the hotter part conducts at a lower gate voltage."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The drain-source body diode drops at most -1.0 V at -1.0 A and carries up to -2.0 A continuously. With -4.0 A forward and 100 A/μs, its recovery charge is 40 to 62 nC and its recovery time 20 to 32 ns."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Dissipation is 1.5 W at 25 °C ambient. The junction-to-ambient resistance is 357 °C/W in steady state on a 1 by 0.85 inch FR-4 board, 0.062 inch thick. Junction and storage temperature both span -55 °C to +150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Trench process in a plastic SOT-23. The mold compound carries a UL 94V-0 flammability rating and is RoHS-compliant and halogen-free; leads are solder plated and pass the MIL-STD-750 method 2026 solderability test."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Offered as a voltage-controlled small-signal switch with fast switching, for battery-powered systems, solid-state relays and direct interfacing to TTL or CMOS logic levels."
  }
 ],
